Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 22:09:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1304/3799] soh: rename D_808BD9C4 -> sUnusedPositions

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: the in-tree comment above it reads "// unused"; the six floats read as two XYZ points and nothing references them.
Defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Bg_Treemouth/z_bg_treemouth.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Bg_Treemouth/z_bg_treemouth.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Bg_Treemouth/z_bg_treemouth.c b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Bg_Treemouth/z_bg_treemouth.c
index 845e6811d..ccda2091b 100644
--- a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Bg_Treemouth/z_bg_treemouth.c
+++ b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Bg_Treemouth/z_bg_treemouth.c
@@ -56,7 +56,8 @@ static InitChainEntry sInitChain[] = {
 };
 
 // unused
-static f32 D_808BD9C4[] = {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was D_808BD9C4: the in-tree comment above it reads "// unused"; the six floats read as two XYZ points and nothing references them.
+static f32 sUnusedPositions[] = {  // was D_808BD9C4 [LLM:HIGH]
     -2746.0f, 545.0f, 4694.0f, -2654.0f, 146.0f, 4534.0f,
 };
 
